<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{@site.locale}}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>{{meta_title}}</title>

    {{!-- FIRST, and inline: sets data-theme before the first paint so a
         dark-mode reader never sees a white flash. See the partial. --}}
    {{> "theme-init"}}

    {{!-- The faces are declared inside namaste-ui.css, which the browser only
         discovers after fetching and parsing screen.css — one round trip later
         than it could start. Preloading closes that gap and is what stops the
         fallback swap being visible on a cold load.

         Only the two files that draw ABOVE THE FOLD are preloaded: the sans
         and the mono. `preload` is a priority instruction, and marking
         everything urgent marks nothing urgent — the icon font is deliberately
         left to be discovered normally, because an icon arriving 100ms late is
         invisible where a reflowing paragraph is not.

         `crossorigin` is required even though these are same-origin: fonts are
         always fetched in CORS mode, and a preload without it produces a
         second, unused download rather than a warm cache hit. --}}
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
          href="{{asset "fonts/switzer-var-latin.woff2"}}">
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
          href="{{asset "fonts/roboto-mono-var-latin.woff2"}}">

    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="{{asset "css/screen.css"}}">

    {{!-- Ghost injects SEO tags, structured data, code injection and Portal.
         It must stay in <head>, and last. --}}
    {{ghost_head}}
  </head>

  <body class="{{body_class}}">
    {{!-- First focusable element on the page; .ns-skip-link is invisible until
         it takes focus. The target carries tabindex="-1" because without it,
         following the link moves the viewport but not focus in Safari and
         Chrome — so the next Tab lands back at the top of the document. --}}
    <a href="#main" class="ns-skip-link">{{t "Skip to content"}}</a>

    {{!-- ── THE CHROME DISPATCH ───────────────────────────────────────────
      default.hbs forks on the SAME tags post.hbs does, so a reading surface
      does not get a marketing bar. abstract/02 is the reference — but the
      NAMES come from abstract/18, which owns the vocabulary and supersedes
      the list abstract/02 was written against (#training-content and
      #training-section were renamed to #training-lesson and
      #training-module; docs gained #docs-page / #docs-section).

      Reading surfaces are therefore: a course lesson, a training lesson, a
      training module overview, a docs page and a docs section overview.
      Everything else — blog, resources, products, untagged — is marketing
      chrome.

      ⚠ BRANCH ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING HERE TOO. `has` takes a comma-separated
      list and matches ANY of them, so this particular fork happens to be
      order-free — but the moment a branch is split out (a section overview
      wanting different chrome from a lesson) the more specific tag must be
      tested FIRST. Same rule, same failure mode, as post.hbs.

      The {{#is "post"}} guard matters: {{#has}} reads tags from the current
      context, and on a listing or a page there are none — so without it every
      non-post route would fall through the wrong side of the fork.
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
    {{#is "post"}}
      {{#post}}
        {{#has tag="#lesson, #training-lesson, #training-module, #docs-page, #docs-section"}}
          {{> "chrome/coursenav"}}
        {{else}}
          {{> "chrome/topnav"}}
        {{/has}}
      {{/post}}
    {{else}}
      {{> "chrome/topnav"}}
    {{/is}}

    {{!-- One sheet serves both bars for now. It sits outside the bar because a
         modal dialog inside a position:sticky ancestor inherits that stacking
         context in some engines and renders under the page it should cover. --}}
    {{> "chrome/nav-sheet"}}

    <main id="main" tabindex="-1">{{{body}}}</main>

    {{#is "post"}}
      {{#post}}
        {{#has tag="#lesson, #training-lesson, #training-module, #docs-page, #docs-section"}}
          {{> "footer-lesson"}}
        {{else}}
          {{> "footer"}}
        {{/has}}
      {{/post}}
    {{else}}
      {{> "footer"}}
    {{/is}}

    {{!-- Deferred: nothing in it is needed for the page to render or be
         usable. Vendored from NS-Design-System unchanged — it drives the
         sheet, the theme controls and the bar's scrolled state by writing the
         aria-* and data-* attributes the CSS already reads. --}}
    <script src="{{asset "js/nav.js"}}" defer></script>

    {{!-- Ghost injects members, search and comments scripts. Keep it last. --}}
    {{ghost_foot}}
  </body>
</html>
